  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through Thursday)\nIssued at 1147 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nThe mid level trough will begin to shift east of the local region\nby Friday evening, though the elongated trough axis will linger in\nthe vicinity through the day Saturday as another weak wave drop\nsoutheast. This will be enough to spark more scattered showers and\npossibly a thunderstorm, mainly south of I-40, through Saturday\nafternoon. Rainfall amount will tend to be light overall with any\nactivity on Saturday as drier air begins to spill into the region.\nA reinforcing cold front drops into the area on Sunday finally\nclearing things out through Sunday afternoon. A modest Canadian\nsurface high will settle into the area through the early part of\nnext week, with some of the coolest overnight lows we have seen \nsince the Spring looking likely. Widespread lows in the 50s will\nbe common the first part of next week, while some of the normally\ncooler locations across the north could dip into the upper 40s,\nespecially Tuesday morning.\n\nTemperatures begin to steadily trend warmer through the latter\npart of the week as mid level ridging builds back stronger over\nthe southwestern CONUS. Highs will climb back into the 80s\nareawide while dry weather prevails through the back half of the\nforecast period.\n\nBowlan",
